    "specPath": "specs/028-opentelemetry-evidence-sink/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Approved (A-24) as its own reviewable change before code. A new optional integration, `integrations/rustev-otel`, exports each delivered run record as OpenTelemetry spans, metrics and optional log records, with GenAI semantic-convention attributes on backend attempts, W3C trace-context parenting from the host, OTLP over gRPC or HTTP to allowlisted host collectors only, and a local JSONL exporter. Every exported field passes a declared redaction policy, `rustev.redaction/1`, that defaults to deny for caller, third-party, attributed-claim and generated text. The policy document, its evaluation, the keyed digest and the `rustev.trace/1` span line document are pure additions to `rustev-contract`; `rustev trace tail` is added to the CLI with no OpenTelemetry dependency; the boundary check gains the telemetry exporter family. Approval does not authorize a release, a deployment, an export to any collector outside tests, or real-user data.\n",
    "title": "OpenTelemetry evidence sink and redaction policy"
  },
